{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ui-settings-004-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TooltipEchoBoxTests.cs", "line": 54, "method": "ResolveCapturedText_IsPureAndRepeatable", "category": "T2", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/UI/TooltipEchoBox.cs:194; make ResolveCapturedText return string.Empty when manualOverride is null -> both red", "what_it_asserts": "Two calls with identical arguments return equal results, and a null override falls back to the GUI tooltip.", "why_weak": "ResolveCapturedText is a pure static over two string arguments, so the repeatability pair compares one expression with itself and cannot red for any realistic change. The third assert is the same observable as ResolveCapturedText_NoOverride_FallsBackToGuiTooltip's InlineData(null) row (line 35).", "proposed_action": "Drop it; purity is a property of the signature here, not a testable behavior. If a determinism guard is still wanted, it belongs on the IMGUI-reading caller (TooltipEchoBox.cs:219), not on the pure resolver.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ui-settings-004-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/FormatCrewManifestTests.cs", "line": 56, "method": "Unchanged_ZeroDelta", "category": "T2", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/UI/RecordingsTableFormatters.cs:285; change the crew delta format string or the sign rule -> both red", "what_it_asserts": "FormatCrewManifest renders an unchanged trait count as 'Pilot: 1 -> 1 (+0)'.", "why_weak": "BothStartAndEnd_ShowsDeltaFormat (line 34) already carries Pilot 1 -> 1 in its fixture and asserts the identical substring, so the zero-delta sign branch is covered there.", "proposed_action": "Drop it, or re-point it at the uncovered shape (a trait present in start but absent from the end dictionary), which is the crew equivalent of the FormatResourceManifest gap filed in ui-settings-003.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
